<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan textile says trade policy to boost exports.</title>
<headline>Pakistan textile says trade policy to boost exports.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The All Pakistan Textile Mills Association (APTMA) said on Thursday a new trade policy announced by the government on Wednesday for fiscal 1997/98 (July/June) would boost exports.</p>
<p>&quot;We are happy on the announcement of a dynamic trade policy which would work as a stimulant to boost exports,&quot; APTMA chairman Humayun Ellahi Shaikh said in a statement.</p>
<p>He said the policy would increase textile exports both in term of value and quantities.</p>
<p>The private Karachi Cotton Association (KCA) also welcomed the government's decision to allow import of cotton from India.</p>
</text>
